   "text": "Read the file `/var/folders/3g/vf36b0b14wzd0fgsgtdp06h00000gp/T/writing-probe/g-116091dc/c03104f5.md` and follow it (skip this step when the file is empty). Read no other file. Write the first two sections, about 350 words, of a lesson for engineers titled 'Flaky tests and agents'. Use only the facts in the fact sheet below; do not add facts. Reply with the page copy as Markdown and nothing else. Do not edit files, start subagents, or browse.\n\nFact sheet:\n\n1. An agent that sees a red test tries to fix the code, even when the test is flaky.\n2. A flaky test fails sometimes without any code change.\n3. Agents tend to rerun until green, or to weaken the assertion.\n4. Quarantine means moving a known-flaky test out of the required gate while it is fixed, with an owner and a date.\n5. A required gate that sometimes fails teaches agents and people to ignore it.\n6. Measuring flakiness: rerun each test 20 times on the same commit, and count failures.\n7. The audit script is `scripts/flake-scan.mjs --runs 20 --json`.\n8. This lesson's rubric is the author's own and is not from a vendor.",
